      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Definition of Noun"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A noun is a naming word used for a person, place, thing, quality, state, or action.",
        "The five fundamental types of nouns are Proper, Common, Collective, Material, and Abstract Nouns.",
        "Nouns are functionally classified as Countable (can be counted) and Uncountable (cannot be counted).",
        "Plural formation follows structural rules based on noun endings (-s, -es, -ies, -ves) or irregular shifts.",
        "Noun gender classifies words into Masculine, Feminine, Common, and Neuter."
      ],
      "id": "wylwg17"
