    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Uncountable nouns (e.g., Furniture, Advice, Information, Scenery) always take a singular verb and cannot be preceded by 'a' or 'an'.",
        "Collective nouns take a singular verb when functioning as a unified group, but a plural verb when individual members act separately.",
        "Nouns that exist in pairs (e.g., Scissors, Trousers, Spectacles) are always plural in form and take plural verbs."
      ],
